# function swapMany(list: Item[], rounds) { .. [list[at], list[other]] = [list[other], list[at]]; list[at] = { name: "x" + round, text: "yy" }; sum += list[at].text.length .. }   the list got an element in front
# The accesses of a swap need one test of the array's storage: the later ones stand behind the first one's yes. A validating build makes the later tests all the same and compares.
# The test compares the whole byte that names the kind of storage, and the lock of the cell lies in that byte. Another thread takes and releases the lock all the while. The storage stays what it was, so the run comes to its end
